{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeUpOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeUpOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramAddCell","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRule"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.upSum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.upSum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L359-L424","doc":"**The up-operator identity.**  `∑_{λ = μ + one addable cell} f^λ = (|μ| + 1) · f^μ`.\n\nStrong induction on `|μ|`.  Each summand is expanded by the branching rule\n(`numSYT_addCell_eq`), the double sum is transposed by `Finset.sum_comm`, and the inner sum is\nidentified with `upSum (μ ∖ c)` (`sum_pairTerm_add`), to which the induction hypothesis applies.\n`card_addableCells_eq_card_cornerCells_succ` then cancels the corner count off both sides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_pairTerm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_pairTerm_add","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L323-L353","doc":"The transposed inner sum: for a removable corner `c`, summing `pairTerm` over all addable cells\nof `μ` recovers `upSum (μ ∖ c)` once the term at `s = c` — which is `f^μ` — is put back. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.numSYT_addCell_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.numSYT_addCell_eq","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L288-L321","doc":"Expanding one summand of `upSum` by the branching rule and splitting off the corner that is the\ncell just inserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.pairTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.pairTerm","kind":"def","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L280-L286","doc":"**The summand of the transposed double sum**, made total in both cells.  It is `f^{(μ ∖ c) + s}`\nwhere that makes sense and `0` elsewhere, so that both orders of summation range over the *full*\n`addableCells μ` and `cornerCells μ` and `Finset.sum_comm` applies with nothing to check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ne_of_addable_of_corner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ne_of_addable_of_corner","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L276-L278","doc":"An addable cell is never a removable corner: the first is outside `μ`, the second inside. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_of_eraseCorner'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_of_eraseCorner'","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L269-L274","doc":"`isAddableCell_of_eraseCorner` with the two cells kept as pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_addCell_iff'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_addCell_iff'","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L262-L267","doc":"`isCornerCell_addCell_iff` with the two cells kept as pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.upSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.upSum","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L258-L260","doc":"`∑_{λ = μ + one addable cell} f^λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.branching_finset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.branching_finset","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L242-L250","doc":"The branching rule, restated as a sum over the `Finset` `cornerCells μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.eraseCornerOrSelf_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.eraseCornerOrSelf_of","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L239-L240","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.eraseCornerOrSelf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.eraseCornerOrSelf","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L234-L237","doc":"**`eraseCorner` made total in the cell**, the mirror of `addCellOrSelf`.  A summand quantified\nover a `Finset` of cells cannot mention `eraseCorner ν c hc`, which needs the corner proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.eraseCorner_addCell_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.eraseCorner_addCell_comm","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L217-L230","doc":"Insertion and corner removal commute at distinct cells: `(μ + s) ∖ c = (μ ∖ c) + s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_of_eraseCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_of_eraseCorner","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L194-L215","doc":"A cell addable to `μ ∖ c`, other than `c` itself, is addable to `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_of_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_of_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L187-L192","doc":"A corner of `μ + s` other than `s` itself was already a corner of `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_addCell_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isCornerCell_addCell_iff","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L137-L177","doc":"**A corner survives an insertion exactly when the inserted cell was addable to the diagram with\nthat corner removed.**\n\nConcretely: inserting `s` destroys the corner `c` precisely when `s` is `c`'s right neighbour or\n`c`'s lower neighbour, and those are exactly the two positions at which `s` fails to be addable to\n`μ ∖ c`.  The proof is the three-case split `a = p` / `a = p + 1` / neither on the row indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_eraseCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_eraseCorner","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L111-L130","doc":"Deleting the corner `(p, q)` shortens row `p` by one and leaves every other row alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L88-L109","doc":"Inserting `(a, b)` lengthens row `a` by one and leaves every other row alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_eq_of_mem_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_eq_of_mem_iff","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungLatticeUpOperator.lean#L74-L86","doc":"A row length is pinned by its membership predicate: if row `i` of `ν` is exactly `{0, …, k-1}`\nthen `ν.rowLen i = k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}